cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MuSA, please cite the paper below (preferred-citation)."
title: "MuSA: Multi-Source variant Annotation"
type: software
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-24"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/davide-scognamiglio/MuSA"
abstract: >-
  MuSA is a Nextflow pipeline that turns germline VCFs into an interpretation-ready MAF and a
  self-contained HTML report. It runs Ensembl VEP and dbNSFP in parallel, merges them into one
  row per variant on the MANE Select transcript, scores every variant with RENOVO 1.5, adds
  ClinVar, ClinGen and HPO context, and ranks the result for clinical review.
keywords:
  - nextflow
  - variant annotation
  - germline
  - clinical genomics
  - rare disease
  - vep
  - dbnsfp
